</div>
          <div class="section__content">
            
            
  <table class="name-value-table" aria-labelledby="headerLineage">
    
  </table>

  
    <h3 class="record-block-section-header">Sources</h3>
    
      <div class="record-block">
        <div class="record-block-header cf">
          <h3 class="left force-break">Nationwide Automatic Identification System</h3>
          <div class="x-small right">CC ID: <span>987304</span></div>
        </div>
        <table class="name-value-table" aria-label="Nationwide Automatic Identification System">
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Contact Role Type:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Originator</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Contact Type:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Organization</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Contact Name:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">U.S. Coast Guard Navigation Center</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Publish Date:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">2019-12-31</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Extent Type:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Range</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Extent Start Date/Time:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">2019-01-01</td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Extent End Date/Time:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">2019-12-31</td>
</tr>
          
          <tr class="ellipsisize">
  <th scope="col">
    Citation URL:
  </th>
  <td><a href="https://www.navcen.uscg.gov/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://www.navcen.uscg.gov/</a></td>
</tr>
          
          
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Source Contribution:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Daily compressed log files containing original AIS messages in NMEA format for the months of January through December for the United States. Authoritative Vessel Identification Service (AVIS) Vessel Catalog.</p>

  </td>
</tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    
  

  
    <h3 class="record-block-section-header">Process Steps</h3>
    
      <div class="record-block">
        <div class="record-block-header cf">
          <h3 class="left">Process Step <span>1</span></h3>
          <div class="x-small right">CC ID: <span>987305</span></div>
        </div>
        <table class="name-value-table" aria-label="Process Step 1">
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Description:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Filter the raw NMEA data to a one-minute sample rate and select a subset of fields using MarineCadastre.gov NMEA to SQL Server processing tools</p>
  <p>Load filtered records to a SQL Server database using MarineCadastre.gov NMEA to SQL Server processing tools</p>
  <p>Conduct quality and completeness check using logging results from the filter and loading process, and database record counts</p>
  <p>Update the IMO, CallSign, VesselName, Length, Width, VesselType, and Draft from US Coast Guard AVIS </p>
  <p>Added or updated the new vessel type code field to each record fragment that was found in the US Coast Guard AVIS</p>
  <p>Export records from the SQL Server database to CSV files organized day of the year using MarineCadastre.gov Filter and Export utilities</p>
  <p>Modify the format of the date and time values to a UTC string format during export</p>
  <p>Modify the format of the IMO vessel number to include the “IMO” prefix during export</p>
  <p>Trim white space from string attributes during export</p>
  <p>Replaced comma punctuation marks with a semi-colon in the vessel name or call sign field if present to improve CSV formatting during export</p>
  <p>Include a header record with descriptive text for each field during export</p>
  <p>Write extracted AIS data to an ASCII CSV format file using MarineCadastre.gov Filter and Export utilities</p>
  <p>Compress each ASCII CSV file</p>

  </td>
</tr>
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Process Date/Time:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">2020-01-01 00:00:00</td>
</tr>
          
          
          
          
          
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
